WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.731 --> 00:06.403 align:center line:79%
As I study the scriptures, I come across
words that really catch my attention,

00:06.837 --> 00:09.773 align:center line:79%
primarily because they have special
meaning as a result

00:09.773 --> 00:12.776 align:center line:81%
of experiences I have had during my life.

00:13.310 --> 00:16.980 align:center line:79%
I spent my career working
as a forensic accountant.

00:17.381 --> 00:18.515 align:center line:81%
With that background, the

00:18.515 --> 00:23.554 align:center line:79%
word “reconcile” has caught my attention
as I read the scriptures.

00:24.054 --> 00:27.090 align:center line:81%
My job was to reconcile reported amounts

00:27.491 --> 00:32.629 align:center line:79%
with financial records by
applying accounting, auditing,

00:32.629 --> 00:34.431 align:center line:81%
and investigative skills.

00:34.665 --> 00:38.035 align:center line:79%
In other words, my goal was to align
the financial reports

00:38.035 --> 00:41.738 align:center line:79%
with the underlying
financial documents to ensure

00:41.772 --> 00:43.407 align:center line:81%
accuracy and validity.

00:43.774 --> 00:46.877 align:center line:79%
I made diligent efforts
to resolve discrepancies,

00:46.877 --> 00:50.447 align:center line:79%
and it was common that significant
time was dedicated

00:50.447 --> 00:53.684 align:center line:79%
to resolving even
very small discrepancies.

00:54.351 --> 00:59.089 align:center line:79%
The Apostle Paul pled with the Corinthians
to be reconciled to God.

01:00.090 --> 01:04.528 align:center line:79%
To be reconciled to God means
to be brought back into harmony with God,

01:04.528 --> 01:09.833 align:center line:79%
or to restore a relationship
with God that has been strained or broken

01:09.833 --> 01:11.969 align:center line:81%
because of our sins or actions.

01:12.336 --> 01:17.040 align:center line:79%
Simply put, being reconciled
to God means aligning our will

01:17.040 --> 01:19.409 align:center line:81%
and actions with God’s will,

01:19.443 --> 01:22.079 align:center line:79%
or, as taught by
President Russell M. Nelson,

01:22.312 --> 01:27.250 align:center line:79%
letting God prevail in our lives.
As taught in the scriptures,

01:27.250 --> 01:29.653 align:center line:81%
we are free to act for ourselves,

01:29.920 --> 01:34.891 align:center line:79%
“to choose the way of everlasting
death or the way of eternal life.”

01:35.192 --> 01:37.194 align:center line:81%
But if we are not diligent,

01:37.527 --> 01:43.500 align:center line:79%
this freedom to act for ourselves may lead
to a loss of alignment with the will

01:43.533 --> 01:49.373 align:center line:79%
of God. The prophet Jacob taught
that when we find ourselves in disharmony

01:49.706 --> 01:51.575 align:center line:81%
or misalignment with God,

01:51.942 --> 01:54.745 align:center line:79%
the only way we can achieve
reconciliation is

01:54.745 --> 01:59.082 align:center line:79%
“to be reconciled unto [God]
through the Atonement of Christ.”

01:59.583 --> 02:03.620 align:center line:79%
We must realize that reconciliation
is dependent on mercy,

02:04.121 --> 02:07.124 align:center line:81%
implying that Jesus Christ's gracious act

02:07.124 --> 02:11.028 align:center line:79%
of Atonement makes
reconciliation possible.

02:11.862 --> 02:13.830 align:center line:81%
As you ponder your own life,

02:14.097 --> 02:18.035 align:center line:79%
think about a time when you
felt distant from Heavenly Father

02:18.235 --> 02:20.871 align:center line:81%
because you had moved away from Him.

02:21.738 --> 02:25.909 align:center line:79%
For instance, perhaps you became
less diligent in your prayers to Him

02:25.909 --> 02:27.944 align:center line:81%
or in keeping His commandments.

02:28.278 --> 02:31.515 align:center line:79%
Just as we choose
to distance ourselves from God,

02:31.515 --> 02:35.352 align:center line:79%
we must choose to initiate
the effort to reconcile.

02:35.752 --> 02:40.857 align:center line:79%
The Lord emphasized our responsibility
when He said, “Draw near unto me,

02:41.291 --> 02:43.260 align:center line:81%
and I will draw near unto you;

02:43.694 --> 02:46.630 align:center line:81%
seek me diligently, and ye shall find me;

02:47.264 --> 02:49.132 align:center line:81%
ask, and ye shall receive;

02:49.499 --> 02:52.302 align:center line:81%
knock, and it shall be opened unto you.”

02:53.303 --> 02:58.041 align:center line:79%
How does the Savior help us restore
and reconcile this important relationship?

02:58.408 --> 03:03.146 align:center line:79%
For me, I make great progress
in my journey to be reconciled to God

03:03.413 --> 03:08.285 align:center line:79%
when I follow the counsel taught by
President Nelson and repent every day,

03:08.852 --> 03:13.990 align:center line:79%
the reason being that reconciliation
signifies the restoration

03:13.990 --> 03:18.729 align:center line:79%
of a broken relationship,
particularly between God and humanity,

03:18.929 --> 03:21.498 align:center line:81%
by removing the barrier of sin.

03:22.365 --> 03:24.935 align:center line:79%
One of the great
reconciliations we read about

03:24.935 --> 03:27.137 align:center line:81%
in the scriptures is that of Enos.

03:27.537 --> 03:30.841 align:center line:79%
Something in his life was out
of alignment with God.

03:31.208 --> 03:36.747 align:center line:79%
He exemplified relying on the Atonement
of Jesus Christ to reconcile with God.

03:37.114 --> 03:41.885 align:center line:79%
He explained his desire to repent,
his humility, his focus,

03:41.885 --> 03:43.453 align:center line:81%
and his determination.

03:43.887 --> 03:49.726 align:center line:79%
His reconciliation with God was confirmed
when a voice came to him saying,

03:49.960 --> 03:54.564 align:center line:79%
“Enos, thy sins are forgiven thee,
and thou shalt be blessed.”

03:54.931 --> 04:00.771 align:center line:79%
Enos recognized the impact that repentance
and reconciliation had on him

04:00.771 --> 04:05.275 align:center line:79%
when he said, “And I, Enos,
knew that God could not lie;

04:05.609 --> 04:07.811 align:center line:81%
wherefore my guilt was swept away.”

04:09.479 --> 04:13.283 align:center line:79%
Reconciliation brings not only
relief from feelings of guilt,

04:13.283 --> 04:16.386 align:center line:79%
but also peace within
ourselves and with others.

04:16.753 --> 04:21.725 align:center line:79%
It heals relationships, softens
hearts, and strengthens our discipleship,

04:21.958 --> 04:24.828 align:center line:81%
bringing increased confidence before God.

04:25.362 --> 04:29.800 align:center line:79%
What brings me great hope and confidence
is another fruit of reconciliation

04:29.800 --> 04:36.106 align:center line:79%
described by Enos when he said,
“And after I, Enos, had heard these words,

04:36.106 --> 04:39.342 align:center line:79%
my faith began to be
unshaken in the Lord.”

04:40.043 --> 04:44.848 align:center line:79%
When I was a boy, my maternal
grandfather had a large cherry orchard.

04:45.348 --> 04:47.751 align:center line:79%
I had the opportunity
to work in the orchard,

04:47.751 --> 04:52.823 align:center line:79%
mostly in the summer during the harvest
of cherries. As a very young boy,

04:52.856 --> 04:55.792 align:center line:79%
the extent of my involvement
was being handed a bucket

04:55.792 --> 04:58.495 align:center line:79%
and then sent up a tree
to pick the cherries.

04:58.962 --> 05:01.832 align:center line:79%
The harvesting of cherries
changed significantly

05:01.832 --> 05:06.970 align:center line:79%
when my grandfather purchased
a machine called a cherry shaker.

05:08.171 --> 05:12.409 align:center line:79%
This machine grabs the trunk
of the tree and shakes it,

05:12.576 --> 05:17.347 align:center line:79%
causing the cherries to fall out
of the tree onto nets that are used

05:17.347 --> 05:18.782 align:center line:81%
to collect the cherries.

05:19.182 --> 05:22.485 align:center line:79%
I noticed that when the shaker
would begin to shake the tree,

05:22.652 --> 05:26.089 align:center line:79%
almost all the cherries fell
out of the tree within seconds.

05:26.389 --> 05:29.726 align:center line:79%
I also noticed that it didn't
matter if the tree was shaken

05:29.726 --> 05:32.229 align:center line:81%
for 10 seconds or a full minute,

05:32.229 --> 05:34.531 align:center line:81%
some cherries would not fall.

05:34.798 --> 05:37.033 align:center line:81%
They were truly unshakable.

05:37.968 --> 05:42.772 align:center line:79%
Shaking cherries out of a tree is possible
because of the release of ethylene.

05:43.340 --> 05:47.911 align:center line:79%
This hormone causes the layer of cells
between the stem of the cherry

05:48.111 --> 05:49.646 align:center line:81%
and the tree to weaken.

05:50.213 --> 05:54.684 align:center line:79%
Therefore, the stem of a ripe cherry
more easily detaches from the tree

05:54.684 --> 05:57.120 align:center line:81%
because of the weakened connection.

05:58.521 --> 06:03.059 align:center line:79%
In the scriptures, we learn
that the Stem of Jesse is a metaphor

06:03.059 --> 06:05.262 align:center line:81%
for the Messiah, Jesus Christ,

06:05.528 --> 06:07.931 align:center line:79%
who was prophesied to
come from the lineage

06:07.931 --> 06:10.901 align:center line:81%
of Jesse, the father of King David.

06:11.101 --> 06:17.173 align:center line:79%
Just as ethylene weakens the connection
of a ripe cherry stem, disobedience,

06:17.173 --> 06:21.711 align:center line:79%
doubts, and fears can weaken
our connection to the Stem of Jesse,

06:22.012 --> 06:27.918 align:center line:79%
or Jesus Christ, allowing us to be easily
shaken and separated from Him.

06:29.085 --> 06:30.620 align:center line:81%
As faithful as we may be,

06:30.654 --> 06:35.091 align:center line:79%
we must guard against a weakening
of our connection to Jesus Christ.

06:35.392 --> 06:37.027 align:center line:81%
In the Doctrine and Covenants,

06:37.027 --> 06:39.362 align:center line:81%
even the faithful are given a warning:

06:39.796 --> 06:43.333 align:center line:79%
“But there is a possibility
that man may fall from grace

06:43.333 --> 06:45.468 align:center line:81%
and depart from the living God.”

06:45.902 --> 06:47.671 align:center line:81%
The Lord continues, “Yes, ...

06:47.671 --> 06:53.310 align:center line:79%
even let those who are sanctified
take heed also.” To avoid falling.

06:53.310 --> 06:58.615 align:center line:79%
the Lord counsels, “therefore let
the church take heed and pray always,

06:58.915 --> 07:01.251 align:center line:81%
lest they fall into temptation.”

07:01.952 --> 07:06.756 align:center line:79%
One might equate the state of being easily
shaken to what scriptures describe

07:06.756 --> 07:12.595 align:center line:79%
as being ripe for destruction,
with impending consequences for actions.

07:13.029 --> 07:17.434 align:center line:79%
The phrase can also be used more broadly
to indicate a state of decay,

07:17.901 --> 07:23.506 align:center line:79%
corruption, or decline that makes
something susceptible to collapse or ruin.

07:24.674 --> 07:26.643 align:center line:81%
What does this ripeness represent?

07:26.643 --> 07:31.348 align:center line:79%
Does it mean that we can reach a point
where we are unable to change?

07:32.148 --> 07:36.653 align:center line:79%
No, I think it means we can reach
a point in time where we are unwilling

07:36.686 --> 07:41.891 align:center line:79%
to change. The antidote
to becoming ripe for destruction is

07:41.891 --> 07:47.630 align:center line:79%
to do those things that will strengthen
our connection to Jesus Christ.

07:47.897 --> 07:52.302 align:center line:79%
As mentioned, repentance led Enos
to the point of unshaken faith.

07:52.736 --> 07:57.574 align:center line:79%
There is strength in repentance—
regular, prompt, and frequent repentance.

07:57.841 --> 08:02.746 align:center line:79%
As President Nelson taught us, “Nothing
is more liberating, more ennobling,

08:02.746 --> 08:08.418 align:center line:79%
or more crucial to our individual
progression than is a regular daily focus

08:08.418 --> 08:11.888 align:center line:81%
on repentance.” In addition to repentance,

08:11.888 --> 08:16.226 align:center line:79%
the prophet Jacob taught that being aware
of God's hand in our lives,

08:16.526 --> 08:18.928 align:center line:81%
seeking and receiving revelation,

08:19.095 --> 08:24.334 align:center line:79%
and listening to God when He speaks
all help us to not be shaken.

08:25.668 --> 08:29.572 align:center line:79%
Jacob also taught
“Wherefore, we search the prophets,

08:29.839 --> 08:33.476 align:center line:79%
and we have many revelations
and the spirit of prophecy;

08:33.877 --> 08:36.279 align:center line:81%
and having all these witnesses,

08:36.513 --> 08:41.084 align:center line:79%
we obtain a hope and our faith
becometh unshaken.”

08:41.518 --> 08:45.555 align:center line:79%
Listening to and acting on the words
and invitations of the prophets

08:45.555 --> 08:50.627 align:center line:79%
and apostles can fill us with hope,
confidence, and strength,

08:50.693 --> 08:53.530 align:center line:81%
resulting in our faith becoming unshaken.

08:54.030 --> 08:57.634 align:center line:79%
I have learned that a desire
to be reconciled

08:57.634 --> 09:02.105 align:center line:79%
to God must be accompanied
by a desire to repent.

09:02.972 --> 09:08.111 align:center line:79%
Repenting and experiencing the blessings
of the Atonement of Jesus Christ

09:08.244 --> 09:10.713 align:center line:81%
leads to unshaken faith.

09:11.381 --> 09:16.286 align:center line:79%
Unshaken faith leads to a desire
to always be reconciled to God.

09:16.519 --> 09:19.956 align:center line:81%
This is a circular or iterative pattern.

09:20.757 --> 09:22.025 align:center line:81%
Brothers and sisters,

09:22.025 --> 09:28.298 align:center line:79%
I invite you to be reconciled to God
through the Atonement of Jesus Christ.

09:28.865 --> 09:31.000 align:center line:81%
I testify that making

09:31.267 --> 09:36.172 align:center line:79%
and keeping covenants makes our connection
to the Savior strong,

09:37.006 --> 09:40.510 align:center line:79%
thereby avoiding becoming ripe
for destruction.

09:40.944 --> 09:43.446 align:center line:81%
I testify that this reconciliation

09:43.446 --> 09:49.486 align:center line:79%
to God through Jesus Christ’s
Atonement leads to unshaken faith.

09:49.953 --> 09:54.691 align:center line:79%
I know Heavenly Father loves you and me,
and He sent His Beloved Son,

09:54.691 --> 10:00.830 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ, to be our Savior,
Redeemer, and the great Reconciler.

10:01.264 --> 10:06.102 align:center line:79%
I testify of Jesus Christ
and do so in the name of Jesus Christ,

10:06.102 --> 10:07.103 align:center line:81%
amen.

